# Context and target selection

Use current evidence to identify each element and its owner. AX supplies unfamiliar context and custom-control actions; already grounded stable fields can use supported semantic locator actions without another AX read. For repeated controls, inspect the relevant group or row together; shared labels and proximity do not prove ownership. A label is not necessarily its input. Qualify checkbox targets by the observed complete accessible name and owner, not nearby text. Read only missing owner-scoped facts. Unknown/protected data, a diff or an excerpt is not evidence of absence.

For additional DOM evidence, `await tab.playwright.domSnapshot()` returns the rendered DOM snapshot, including expanded iframe bodies when available. When an excerpt answers the question, label it as such and bound emitted text: `output.write({ kind: 'DOM excerpt (not the whole page)', text: (await tab.playwright.domSnapshot()).slice(0, 6000) })`. Slicing bounds output, not capture work, and an arbitrary excerpt cannot prove uniqueness or completion. For a narrow known question, prefer a grounded locator's `count()`, `isVisible()`, `isEnabled()`, `textContent()`, approved non-sensitive `getAttribute()` or selected-value state; use full AX/diff only when context is needed. Selectors must come from observed structure, labels or attributes; do not guess IDs or use position as identity.

## Tab readiness

`listTabs()` may expose `initialization.status/stage/reason` and `navigationWait.status/stage/elapsedMs`. Discovery is not renderer readiness; document readiness is not application completion. For a pending child or `BROWSER_NOT_READY`, inspect that tab and its dialog, not the opener. Surface failed initialization's safe reason. A protocol-failed tab may close; confirm absence in `listTabs()` before opening a separately authorized destination. Never repeat Continue/open merely because a read or wait failed. Verify destination application state separately. Crashes/pending work: [recovery](stable-recovery.md).

## Form information and approval

Before asking for user information, inspect the complete visible required form schema together: labels, required/conditional fields, constraints and missing values, including postal code. Relay that complete schema to the coordinator in one request; do not assume it can infer omitted fields. Request jointly needed username and password together through the secure form. Reuse a supplied route/access link; request another only after evidence that it is missing or unusable. Keep secrets out of ordinary messages and observations.

After Next/submit, verify the destination or validation errors before reporting progress/blockers. Request accuracy-declaration approval only from its actual control, complete accessible name and owner in current evidence.

Before final order/payment approval, verify the requested item, total, relevant terms and specified stored card identity: match every user-specified identity attribute against its displayed saved label, brand and/or last digits, not a generic payment-method label. Resolve missing/mismatched identity before approval or commit. Never expose full card details or repeat approval already covering the unchanged action. Use the [protected-input workflow](stable-universal.md#protected-inputs-and-uploads).

## Bounded read-only inspection

`tab.playwright.evaluate(fn,arg?,{timeoutMs?})` returns the JSON value directly. Locator `evaluate` receives the matched element; `evaluateAll` receives the matches. Functions cannot access outer variables, state, iab, output or Node. Pass the required JSON argument explicitly. These methods are read-only: do not mutate the DOM, storage or network or attempt to bypass their policy. They inspect the live owner; they do not validate stale AX indexes or turn an ambiguous owner into a safe mutation target.

### Timeout state summary

After target/preparation errors, preserve native `cause`/`stage` and intent/error; see [classification](stable-locator-recovery.md). `Current locator state` is supplemental: counts and up to five structural candidates, no page text/values. It describes current layout/own-disabled state, not the original cause, hit-test success, occlusion or full actionability. A later diagnostic error must not replace the original failure. Inspect only missing facts on the same grounded locator:

```js
const summary = { count: await expected.count() }
if (summary.count === 1) {
  summary.visible = await expected.isVisible()
  summary.enabled = await expected.isEnabled()
}
output.write(summary)
```

Correct the observed cause, then reacquire and resume only the remaining authorized action; a successful diagnostic read is not its completion. Never repeat an unchanged wait without new evidence, transition or revised deadline. Never replay successful/uncertain input or resubmit payment to recover a wait.

### Raw-selector policy

Inside the `evaluate` membrane, raw `querySelector`, `querySelectorAll`, `matches` and `closest` reject CSS attribute predicates such as `input[type=number]`, including public attributes. This protects against a raw-value oracle; it is not merely a mutation restriction. Do not retry the same prohibited expression or fall back to universal/CDP evaluation to evade it.

Instead, ground `observedSelector` in current evidence and resolve it outside the membrane with `tab.playwright.locator(observedSelector)`, then inspect only known non-sensitive fields through locator `evaluate` or `evaluateAll`:

```js
const control = state.tab.playwright.locator(observedSelector)
output.write(
  await control.evaluate((element) => ({
    disabled: element.getAttribute('aria-disabled'),
    selected: element.getAttribute('aria-selected'),
    text: (element.textContent || '').slice(0, 500),
  })),
)
```

The callback remains read-only and credential-redacting. This is not a bypass: never use it to read arbitrary attributes or secret fields; keep protected inputs on their dedicated workflow.

After observing the region's label, inspect its non-sensitive state:

```js
const group = state.tab.playwright.getByRole('group', {
  name: 'Item X',
  exact: true,
})
output.write(
  await group.evaluate((element) => ({
    label: element.getAttribute('aria-label'),
    expanded: element.getAttribute('aria-expanded'),
    selected: element.getAttribute('aria-selected'),
    text: (element.textContent || '').slice(0, 500),
  })),
)
```

Match controls through explicit labels, controls/description relationships, form ownership or observed row identity. Missing or ambiguous links require more evidence, not first/nth. Re-read affected context after effects and verify actual application state, not merely dispatch success.

Use `frameLocator(observedSelector)` for iframe content and chain it for nested frames. Frame entry, locator matching and actionability checks run when the locator is used. Locator builders do not themselves establish that a match exists.

At a point from a displayed viewport screenshot, `tab.playwright.elementInfo({x,y})` returns selector-oriented metadata; `elementScreenshot({x,y})` returns a cropped image of the visible hit-tested element for `output.image`. Crops do not establish coordinates or replace the displayed viewport's coordinate binding. Image references are not screenshot bytes. Both methods reject `includeNonInteractable`; omit it. Read `iab.help('playwright')` for supported parameters.

# tab.playwright

Generated from the enabled engine members in codex-app/api.json with Manus runtime adaptations.

Locators are lazy selector builders. Reads and actions resolve the selector afresh. evaluate is read-only: no DOM, storage or network mutation. Arm waitForEvent before the triggering action and await its result afterwards. expectNavigation arms before running its callback. Point inspection accepts only x and y and returns the hit-tested element.

Manus returns opaque image references, not byte arrays. Display them with output.image(image). Only displayed viewport screenshots establish coordinates; element crops do not replace that binding. ax.write("screenshot") displays directly.

```ts
type BrowserImageReference = { ref: string; descriptor: unknown };
```

```ts
interface PlaywrightAPI {
  domSnapshot(): Promise<string>; // Return a snapshot of the current DOM as a string, including expanded iframe body content when available.
  elementInfo(options: ElementInfoOptions): Promise<Array<ElementInfo>>; // Return locator-oriented metadata for elements at a screenshot coordinate.
  elementScreenshot(options: ElementScreenshotOptions): Promise<BrowserImageReference>; // Return a cropped image of the visible hit-tested element; it is not a coordinate capture.
  evaluate<TResult, TArg>(pageFunction: PlaywrightEvaluateFunction<TArg, TResult>, arg?: TArg, options?: PlaywrightEvaluateOptions): Promise<TResult>; // Evaluate JavaScript in a read-only page scope.
  expectNavigation<T>(action: () => Promise<T>, options: { timeoutMs?: number; url?: string; waitUntil?: LoadState }): Promise<T>; // Expect a navigation triggered by an action.
  frameLocator(frameSelector: string): PlaywrightFrameLocator; // Create a frame-scoped locator builder.
  getByLabel(text: TextMatcher, options: { exact?: boolean }): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by label text within the page.
  getByPlaceholder(text: TextMatcher, options: { exact?: boolean }): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by placeholder text within the page.
  getByRole(role: string, options: { exact?: boolean; name?: TextMatcher }): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by ARIA role within the page.
  getByTestId(testId: string): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by test id within the page.
  getByText(text: TextMatcher, options: { exact?: boolean }): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by text within the page.
  locator(selector: string): PlaywrightLocator; // Create a locator scoped to this tab.
  waitForEvent(event: "download", options?: WaitForEventOptions): Promise<PlaywrightDownload>; // Wait for the next download to complete; call before clicking its download control.
  waitForEvent(event: "filechooser", options?: WaitForEventOptions): Promise<PlaywrightFileChooser>; // Wait for a file chooser.
  waitForLoadState(options: PageWaitForLoadStateOptions): Promise<void>; // Wait for the page to reach a specific load state.
  waitForTimeout(timeoutMs: number): Promise<void>; // Wait for a fixed duration.
  waitForURL(url: string, options: PageWaitForURLOptions): Promise<void>; // Wait for the page URL to match the provided value.
}

type ElementInfoOptions = {
  x: number;
  y: number;
};

type ElementInfo = {
  ariaName?: string | null; // Accessible name if available.
  boundingBox?: ElementInfoRect | null; // Element bounds in screenshot coordinates.
  nodeId?: number | null; // Backend node id that can be passed to DOM-inspection APIs when available.
  preview: string; // Compact human-readable node preview.
  role?: string | null; // Computed ARIA role if available.
  selector: ElementInfoSelector; // Suggested selector data for this element.
  tagName: string; // Lowercased HTML tag name.
  testId?: string | null; // Configured test id attribute if present.
  visibleText?: string | null; // Rendered visible text, selected option text, or visible form value when available.
};

type ElementInfoRect = {
  height: number;
  width: number;
  x: number;
  y: number;
};

type ElementInfoSelector = {
  candidates: Array<string>; // Ranked selector candidates for the element.
  frameSelectors?: Array<string>; // Frame selectors to enter before using the element selector.
  primary?: string | null; // The preferred selector for the element when available.
};

type ElementScreenshotOptions = {
  x: number;
  y: number;
};

type PlaywrightEvaluateFunction<TArg, TResult> = string | (arg: TArg) => TResult | Promise<TResult>;

type PlaywrightEvaluateOptions = {
  timeoutMs?: number; // Maximum time to spend setting up the read-only DOM scope and running the script.
};

type LoadState = "load" | "domcontentloaded" | "networkidle";

type TextMatcher = string | RegExp;

type WaitForEventOptions = {
  timeoutMs?: number;
};

type PageWaitForLoadStateOptions = {
  state?: LoadState;
  timeoutMs?: number;
};

type PageWaitForURLOptions = {
  timeoutMs?: number;
  waitUntil?: WaitUntil;
};

type WaitUntil = LoadState | "commit";
```
